{"k": "8c9be7e43f22234e1cc11a68c715cd52", "v": 1.0, "resp": "**Attributable**\n\nThe reference directly states that lipid nanoparticles form a biomolecular corona of plasma proteins upon exposure to biological fluids. This directly supports the claim that lipid nanoparticles form a protein corona when exposed to biological fluids (a corona of plasma proteins is a protein corona)."}
{"k": "f89ed2e4a5fd8edcc5b8e0017f848907", "v": 0.0, "resp": "**Extrapolatory**\n\nThe reference discusses quantum dots and their size-dependent photoluminescence. It provides no information about lipid nanoparticles, protein coronas, or biological fluids. Therefore, the claim cannot be verified from this reference."}
